<title>SINGAPORE: Pertamina increases Minas allocations in Sept.</title>
<headline>Pertamina increases Minas allocations in Sept.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-08-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Indonesia's state oil company, Pertamina has allocated 49,000 barrels-per-day (bpd) of Minas export crude for September lifting, down from 38,000 bpd in August, traders said on Monday.  </p>
<p>But a slow startup at Indonesia's Humpuss condensate splitter led to increased availabilities of Arun condensate, which will be used as feedstock at the splitter.</p>
<p>The 70,000-bpd condensate splitter started test runs at the end of July, but was not operating at full capacity yet.</p>
<p>Industry sources said Pertamina made the following allocations: (Figures are in barrels per day)</p>
<p>	  September   August    July	June	May</p>
<p>MINAS    49,000     38,000  52,000    62,000    73,000</p>
<p>DURI     31,000     31,000  20,000    33,000    60,000</p>
<p>WIDURI   17,000     48,000  17,000    28,000    18,000</p>
<p>CINTA     4,000     35,000  17,000     4,000    14,000</p>
<p>ARUN     22,000     20,000   none	 none    24,000</p>
<p>BELIDA    6,000     15,000  30,000     6,000    10,000</p>
<p>B. MIX   28,000     35,000  28,000    18,000    35,000</p>
